==Drops==
{{Listen|align=right|filename=Giant mole kill.ogg|title=You have defeated the giant mole.|desc=}}
{{DropLogProject|jagex=yes}}
After fighting the mole, it is decided if a rare unique item will be dropped, and what that item is, before attributing it to a player. The odds of any rare item dropping at all are 1/10. After it is determined that a rare item will drop, which specific item is to be dropped is determined using a 52-slot table. This rare item is then distributed to one of the top three players, or to the single player if fighting the mole solo.{{CiteForum|url=http://services.runescape.com/m=forum/forums.ws?74,75,52,65949497,goto,18#177|author=Mod Shauny|title=Dev Blog: Revealing Drop Rates|postdate=3 November 2017|forum=Existing Game Content|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/100602|archivedate=3 November 2017|name=revealed rates}} All of the mole's special drops ([[clingy mole]]s, [[numbing root]]s, [[dragon 2h sword]]s, and [[ultra-growth potion]]s) are tertiary drops. Whenever someone receives a special drop from the mole, it will be announced in the [[message box]].

The drop mechanics for the mole function differently in a group than when fought solo. Namely, the player to deal the most damage will always receive [[big bones]] and a [[mole claw]] if on a members' world, or only big bones if on a F2P world; the three players to deal the most damage will receive three [[mole skin]]s, distributed equally (if the group is two players, there is a random chance for either player to receive two, and the other will receive one), all players who have completed the [[Falador achievements#Elite achievements|elite Falador achievement set]] will receive a [[mole nose]], and players doing the [[Fur 'n Seek]] wishlist will sometimes receive [[long, sharp claws]]. The regular item drops are then divided equally between the top 3 players; if the drop quantity does not divide equally, the remainder is given to a random player of the top three that did not receive a rare drop.

In hard mode, rare unique drops are more common, while some items are dropped in larger quantities.

Following the 27 January 2014 update, the giant mole no longer has access to the [[rare drop table]].

