==Trivia==
* The Giant Mole received a graphical and mechanical update on [[27 January]] [[2014]]. The same update also reduced the cavern size by half. Details about the mole before her update can be found [[Giant Mole (historical)|here]].
* Sometimes, a glitch can occur where the giant mole may stay in one room for two phases rather than constantly moving around as her life points deplete. This only occurs when she first tunnels away to the first cavern.
* The giant mole was made available to [[free-to-play]] players on [[29 February]] [[2016]]. The same update also removed the shortcut areas in the cavern into gaps wide enough for players to run through.
* As of [[1 February]] [[2018]], the highest kill count for this boss was 2,775 kills for normal mode and 2,670 for hard mode.{{CiteReddit|author=Mod Shauny|url=https://www.reddit.com/r/runescape/comments/7uqej0/top_10_killers_per_boss/|title=Top 10 killers per Boss|quote=Here are the top 10 kills for each Boss in RuneScape, be aware that we've not listed display names for privacy purposes however if you wish to brag about one number being yours then we won't stop you!|date=2 February 2018|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/102945|archivedate=25 January 2019}}
** This had increased to 5,000 for normal mode and 5,130 for hard mode by [[13 December]] [[2018]].{{CiteReddit|author=Mod Shauny|url=https://www.reddit.com/r/runescape/comments/adugze/top_20_boss_killers_by_monster_data_13th_december/|title=Top 20 Boss Killers by Monster (Data: 13th December 2018)|quote=[link to a spreadsheet]|date=8 January 2019|archiveurl=http://archive.is/ycOt4|archivedate=28 February 2020}}
* The giant mole's scientific name, ''Talpidae wysonian'', is a reference to the real life {{WP|Talpidae}} family of moles.
* The giant mole's carcass serves as the mining node for the [[Croesus]] boss encounter.
* In a [[18 May]] [[2026]] blog post, a Giant Mole rework was joked about, renaming the boss '''Micro Mole''', along with other changes intended to make the encounter more annoying. The blog post ended with {{RSFont|*none of these changes are actually planned or will go live.}} written in small text.{{CiteNews|author=|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/daemonheim-drift---hiscores-now-live|title= Daemonheim Drift - Hiscores now live!|newsdate=18 May 2026|notes=|name=}}

